# Engine objects that reference a symbol only a shell object defines.
#
# EMPTY, and it stays that way. The engine reads its options from a snapshot it
# is handed, renders its own text, and says things through the output sink --
# function pointers the host registers, with a printing default -- so no engine
# object needs a symbol the shell defines.
#
# There is no debt left to grandfather here, so the next entry to appear is the
# first, and it fails the gate rather than joining a list.
